WEBVTT

00:00.280 --> 00:02.680
How much time goes into organising a working day?

00:03.080 --> 00:03.880
You have the people.

00:04.160 --> 00:04.900
You have the work.

00:05.340 --> 00:09.600
Now everyone needs to know where to go, who to travel with and where they are staying.

00:09.980 --> 00:11.500
The shift changed in the chat.

00:11.840 --> 00:14.180
The spreadsheet, of course, still has its own version.

00:14.540 --> 00:16.459
And here come the same questions again.

00:16.960 --> 00:19.540
Let’s bring the assignments together in JobHub Support.

00:19.860 --> 00:23.400
The manager prepares the work, and each person sees their own schedule.

00:24.140 --> 00:25.900
What is happening in the company right now?

00:26.600 --> 00:29.240
Usually, finding out starts with a few phone calls.

00:29.800 --> 00:34.500
Here are your team, projects, shifts, requests and hours waiting for review.

00:34.980 --> 00:36.360
You can see what needs attention.

00:36.860 --> 00:39.040
And the worker has their own schedule on the phone.

00:39.380 --> 00:42.480
They check the published shift, rather than hunt for it in the chat.

00:43.280 --> 00:44.380
The team is growing.

00:44.840 --> 00:46.760
How do you connect a new person to the company?

00:47.340 --> 00:49.340
First, send an email invitation.

00:49.760 --> 00:52.260
The worker accepts it in their own JobHub account.

00:52.720 --> 00:56.080
Once they are connected, open their profile and check their assignments.

00:56.500 --> 00:59.660
The owner decides who looks after what and who has access.

01:00.140 --> 01:03.340
One manager handles their team; another handles different work.

01:03.780 --> 01:05.640
Everyone has a clear part to play.

01:06.580 --> 01:07.700
You changed the schedule.

01:08.000 --> 01:08.820
Does everyone know?

01:09.500 --> 01:12.060
A message in the chat does not always do the job.

01:12.680 --> 01:17.420
In the project, choose the crew, the people and the dates, then publish the shifts.

01:17.920 --> 01:21.680
The worker gets their shift for the day, the place of work and the start time.

01:22.040 --> 01:23.520
The manager prepares the day.

01:23.900 --> 01:25.900
The worker knows where to be and when.

01:26.560 --> 01:27.660
The shift is sorted.

01:28.020 --> 01:29.900
Now, who is travelling with whom?

01:30.720 --> 01:34.340
Here are the driver, the vehicle and the passengers for the right dates.

01:34.780 --> 01:37.840
If the group changes, check the seats and arrange a replacement.

01:38.320 --> 01:40.800
The calendar has two weeks of weekdays selected.

01:41.240 --> 01:44.140
Set the shift times and publish the schedule for those days.

01:44.580 --> 01:46.760
Plan the ride alongside the working days.

01:47.860 --> 01:49.500
Someone new is arriving tomorrow.

01:49.940 --> 01:50.800
Where will they stay?

01:51.480 --> 01:52.540
Open accommodation.

01:53.160 --> 01:57.420
See who is already there, which places are taken and who is next to move in.

01:57.940 --> 02:00.320
Check the planned departures and assign a place.

02:00.820 --> 02:02.640
Now you can see where the person will stay.

02:03.160 --> 02:06.280
If plans change, cancel the move-in and keep the history.

02:07.080 --> 02:08.540
Remember that day-off request?

02:08.900 --> 02:11.920
It is somewhere between a photo and ten other messages.

02:12.340 --> 02:14.460
Here, it arrives as a separate request.

02:14.820 --> 02:18.780
The manager reads it, asks for any details in the chat and makes a decision.

02:19.200 --> 02:21.300
The worker sees the status and the answer.

02:21.760 --> 02:23.640
No need to wonder whether anyone noticed.

02:24.520 --> 02:26.380
You need to explain something about work.

02:26.780 --> 02:28.300
Shall we switch to another app again?

02:28.880 --> 02:31.260
Here, the conversation is beside the work.

02:31.820 --> 02:34.100
Send a message, a photo or a screenshot.

02:34.480 --> 02:36.300
Keep reminders in your private notes.

02:36.580 --> 02:37.740
Only you can see them.

02:38.260 --> 02:39.360
Need to connect two people?

02:39.760 --> 02:43.280
Share a contact, and the other person can open the profile to get in touch.

02:44.200 --> 02:45.380
You sent the instruction.

02:45.740 --> 02:47.460
Was it done, or just read?

02:48.160 --> 02:49.960
Assign the task to the right people.

02:50.420 --> 02:53.600
The worker reports it done; the manager checks the result.

02:54.220 --> 02:56.760
If something needs changing, return it with a comment.

02:57.420 --> 02:59.660
Choose who receives important announcements too.

03:00.180 --> 03:03.680
And, where acknowledgement is enabled, see who has confirmed they read it.

03:04.460 --> 03:05.420
The shift is over.

03:05.760 --> 03:07.800
How many hours did everyone actually work?

03:08.500 --> 03:11.760
The worker enters their hours on the phone and sends them for review.

03:12.180 --> 03:14.940
The manager compares them with the schedule and confirms them.

03:15.340 --> 03:19.840
If something does not match, return the entry with a comment explaining what needs correcting.

03:20.580 --> 03:26.780
Here is the whole week, person by person: planned hours, worked hours and entries still waiting for review.

03:27.200 --> 03:29.060
The manager knows what is left to check.

03:29.360 --> 03:31.540
The worker knows what is happening with their hours.

03:32.540 --> 03:35.300
What if you are on site and the computer is back at the office?

03:35.740 --> 03:37.920
You can sort out a small question from your phone.

03:38.520 --> 03:40.700
Open a worker’s request and make a decision.

03:41.280 --> 03:44.920
Check submitted hours, confirm them or return them for correction.

03:45.460 --> 03:47.660
Message the person and clear up the details.

03:48.100 --> 03:49.940
Take a quick look at what needs attention.

03:50.460 --> 03:52.940
Open a worker’s profile and check their assignments.

03:53.420 --> 03:55.440
Check the crew and the working day you need.

03:55.940 --> 03:58.040
Check accommodation and available places.

03:58.480 --> 04:00.420
The computer is handy for the main work.

04:00.760 --> 04:02.840
For a quick question, you do not always need it.

04:03.200 --> 04:06.220
What you can do depends on the access the owner has given you.

04:06.920 --> 04:07.880
The hours are checked.

04:08.200 --> 04:10.960
Time to pass them to the accountant or prepare a report.

04:11.480 --> 04:17.340
Here is the file: workers, projects, working days, planned hours and the time actually worked.

04:17.860 --> 04:19.960
Choose the period and download its totals.

04:20.519 --> 04:22.460
Need a different format or set of columns?

04:22.880 --> 04:25.980
Let’s discuss it and agree what fits the way your company works.

04:26.880 --> 04:29.180
Shall we try this with a working situation you know?

04:29.620 --> 04:33.260
Put a team together, prepare a shift, a ride and a place to stay.

04:33.700 --> 04:36.740
See what the worker gets and how the manager checks the hours.

04:37.400 --> 04:39.200
Does your company work a little differently?

04:39.580 --> 04:40.320
Tell us about it.

04:40.620 --> 04:43.620
We are happy to discuss extra features that would help your team.

04:44.080 --> 04:45.360
Request a demo trial.

04:45.680 --> 04:49.100
We will get to know how your team works and choose where to start together.
